# Hyperdrive org graph

This checkout is `hyperdrive-technology/starfleet`. GitHub still uses the Starfleet names. Packages ship as `@holodeck/*`. Holodeck is the HMI and scene layer. Hyperdrive is the control runtime.

## Sibling repos (`hyperdrive-technology/`)

| Repo | Role |
|------|------|
| `starfleet` | Browser HMI monorepo. `@holodeck/cli`, `@holodeck/editor-2d-react`, `@holodeck/viewer-3d-react`. Scene tooling and live overlays only. |
| `starfleet-sdk` | `@holodeck/sdk` contracts. SceneFile, Importer, Provider, AnimationHook, JSON Schema. Open packages depend on this only. |
| `starfleet-provider-hyperdrive` | Live Hyperdrive runtime data for diagrams (WS/HTTP bridge to variables, alarms, scan timing, diagnostics). |
| `starfleet-provider-otel` | Live OTEL / Prometheus data for diagrams. |
| `starfleet-gateway-grafana` | Proxies Grafana LGTM (Loki, Prometheus, Tempo) for the OTEL provider. |
| `turso-timeseries` | Rust Turso time-series extension (hypertables, line protocol, WASM ext). Historian-adjacent storage. Not HMI. |
| `aws-controllers-k8s-proxy` | AWS ACK proxy. |
| `core` (private) | Hyperdrive runtime, compiler, host API, `core/gateway`. Rust native services live here. Holodeck does not run PLC scan logic. |

GitHub URLs follow `https://github.com/hyperdrive-technology/<repo>`. Docs may still say `holodeck`, `holodeck-sdk`, or `holodeck-provider-*`. Those names map to the Starfleet repos above.

## Ownership

- Hyperdrive (`core`) owns control, compile, deploy, and the host API (port 4444).
- Holodeck (`starfleet` + SDK + providers) owns scene tooling and live overlays.
- Providers and gateways implement `@holodeck/sdk` interfaces. They do not hard-depend on `@holodeck-pro/*`.
- Commercial / gated assets stay in private `holodeck-pro` if it exists. Do not invent that tree in these OSS repos.

## Live values stay IEC tails

Do not invent, copy, or commit live process values, production credentials, customer endpoints, or runtime tag snapshots into these repos.

Those live values stay in IEC tails (the Hyperdrive / IEC 61131 runtime and its historian). Scene files and provider code may name tags or aliases. They must not embed live readings or secrets.

If a task needs a live value, read it from the runtime or an IEC tail. Do not fabricate one.
